WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:04.759
Film Courage:&nbsp; Peter, what makes a good story?

00:00:04.759 --> 00:00:06.700
Peter Russell:&nbsp; Embarrassment.&nbsp;

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.069
Truth.&nbsp;

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:16.320
Ask yourself (and you do it alone in a room),
write down on a piece of paper, the ten most

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:22.640
embarrassing things (secrets) in your life
you would never want anyone to know.&nbsp;

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:28.000
Now we all have them, write down ten of them…you
don’t ever want to show this to anybody,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.710
you don’t have to.&nbsp;

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:37.220
But those ten embarrassing secrets will fuel
almost all the stories you’re ever going

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.660
to tell in your life.&nbsp;

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:45.909
Every story you tell if going to come out
of those horrible embarrassments because they

00:00:45.909 --> 00:00:50.430
are what’s wounded you and they start when
you’re little and it’s usually our parents

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.929
that wound us.&nbsp;

00:00:51.929 --> 00:00:57.289
Sometimes it’s a dirty ole’ uncle, sometimes
it’s a neighbor, but it’s usually our

00:00:57.289 --> 00:00:58.300
parents.&nbsp;

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:03.050
So if you can understand what those wounds
are, you’re going to be able to write ten

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:10.630
compelling characters all having behaviors
that are compensations for that wound.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:14.840
Like I said, one of mine was that my Mommy
didn’t love me, but it came out in Body

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.729
Dysmorphia, that won’t be the case for you.&nbsp;

00:01:17.729 --> 00:01:21.579
The one wound – “I’m unlovable,” look
how it worked for Don Draper (AMC’s television

00:01:21.579 --> 00:01:22.579
series Mad Men).&nbsp;

00:01:22.579 --> 00:01:24.409
He became Mr. Handsome.&nbsp;

00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:26.770
Everything he did was seductive.&nbsp;

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:27.829
Yes?&nbsp;

00:01:27.829 --> 00:01:32.869
So that’s a difference, because everyone
is different to how they react to the core

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:35.149
wound.&nbsp;

00:01:35.149 --> 00:01:40.090
This is the most potent way to tell a great
story and it’s about character.&nbsp;

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:45.429
You know, Blake Snyder, wrote a great book
called SAVE THE CAT, but he didn’t talk

00:01:45.429 --> 00:01:47.369
much about character.&nbsp;

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:52.109
And so this lecture I gave yesterday which
was killing the cat is sort of like what else

00:01:52.109 --> 00:01:57.829
you need to know about story if you want to
write a compelling story today.&nbsp;

00:01:57.829 --> 00:02:03.890
Character is something that seems like a black
box for a lot of writers.&nbsp;

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:09.520
So I’m suggesting what’s more interesting
in your life than what happened to you?&nbsp;

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.310
Your secrets.&nbsp;

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:15.800
If you can’t get interested in your own
secrets, you are going to write a boring character.&nbsp;

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:21.140
Or sometimes you see teachers say “Here
is a list of things.&nbsp;

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:26.560
Write down a list of character attributes,
Well they like tea, they like…I don’t

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:27.560
know…diapers.”&nbsp;

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.390
It seems so arbitrary, right?&nbsp;

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.150
Who cares?&nbsp;

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:37.220
Think about your own wound, you like what
you have avoided and what you still avoid.&nbsp;

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.780
And I guarantee, “…Like she’s gonna
really say that?&nbsp;

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.980
I don’t want to reveal that about myself.”&nbsp;

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.120
Well, you’re going to have a boring story
if you don’t and even writers who are very

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.970
successful and they tell me “I never do
any of that crap.&nbsp;

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:53.620
I’m completely unanalyzed and I don’t
need analysis.&nbsp;

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:59.519
One page of their script reveals reveals all
of that damage, whether they want it to or

00:02:59.519 --> 00:03:00.519
not.&nbsp;

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:01.519
It’s right there.&nbsp;

00:03:01.519 --> 00:03:02.069
It’s what they write about.

